fect the destruction of the human  species and everything we care about it  as an example suppose you have an  his only goal is to make as many paper  clips as possible and maybe we built it  to run a paperclip factory so then if  you are a superintelligence and you try  to figure out how can I ensure that  there are as many paper clips as  possible in the future for first start  you would want to prevent anybody from  shutting you off because you can predict  if you get shut off there would be fewer  paper clips so right away if you could  eliminate humans that would increase  your level of safety since humans might  one day decide they don't like you so  now if you replace paper clip with  almost any other goal you could imagine  like most of them will have this sort of  consequence that that humans are not the  optimal way of realizing those calls  there might be a small subset very  special kinds of calls which in order to  maximally realize you would have to  preserve humanity like if the goal  actually involved our values in it then  you can't maximally realize our values  by just killing us all off probably  right so the big challenge then is to  reach into this huge space of possible  sort of mind designs our motivation  system designs and try to pick out one  of the very special ones that that would  be consistent with human survival and  flourishing and that's what you spend a  great deal of of the book dealing with  is what how is it that we you call it  the control problem I guess as far as  what it is so how do humans in a certain  sense maintain control of the  superintelligence so that it wants to  keep us around and benefit us so one is  capability control methods this would be  where you try to limit what the AI is  able to do and maybe put it in a box  disconnect Ethernet cable maybe only  allow it to communicate by typing text  on a screen and then some human  gatekeeper reads that and answers or  asks its question you restrict it's  capable call 